  "Number": 21,
  "Question": "Mr. Green receives a \\(10\\%\\) raise every year. His salary after four such raises has gone up by what percent?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "less than \\(40\\%\\)",
    "B": "\\(40\\%\\)",
    "C": "\\(44\\%\\)",
    "D": "\\(45\\%\\)",
    "E": "more than \\(45\\%\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Measure salary in units equal to \\(1\\%\\) of Mr. Green's original salary, so his starting salary is \\(100\\) units. Each raise adds \\(10\\%\\) of his current salary, making the new salary \\(1.1\\) times the previous salary.\n\nAfter the four raises, his salary in these units is successively\n\\[\n110,\\quad 121,\\quad 133.1,\\quad 146.41.\n\\]\nThus the increase is \\(146.41-100=46.41\\) units out of the original \\(100\\), or \\(46.41\\%\\). This is more than \\(45\\%\\), so the answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
